            "creator": "michaelchirico4",
            "bug_id": 19125,
            "text": "Created attachment 3775\nExpress tz offset in seconds and thereby avoid truncation error\n\n```\nstrptime(\"2020-01-01 -0001\", \"%Y-%m-%d %z\", tz = \"UTC\")\n# [1] \"2020-01-01 00:00:36 UTC\"\n```\n\nThe problem is the `/30` is truncated to integer. We can overcome this by moving the `*3600/100` step earlier and avoiding `/` as much as possible.\n\nIn fact, I think it's much more natural to express this calculation in the units of seconds, as in the patch, but I may be missing a subtlety.",
